rebuild-history-projections-from-paginated-rollouts

Lane: backend

Unit: rebuild-sqlite-history-from-paginated-rollouts

ChildPatch: rebuild-history-projections-from-paginated-rollouts

Form: GitDiff

Segment: none

Purpose: Forcibly rebuild SQLite history from selected already-paginated rollouts and recover indexed session titles without converting legacy rollouts or changing paginated bytes.

Requires: Unit:normalization/route-thread-writer-locks-to-harness

Provides: Expose codex rebuild-rollout-index using upstream migrate-rollouts arguments and progress interaction with the shared projection engine. Rebuild every selected paginated projection, skip legacy JSONL unchanged, inspect skipped legacy files and missing paginated indexes without database mutation, reconcile missing metadata, and preserve compressed bytes and history-base ordinals. Restore indexed titles into missing startup rows and prune stale names only after complete successful scans.

Boundary: Legacy conversion remains exclusively in ordinary migrate-rollouts and startup; neither forces existing paginated projections. The name index stays under CODEX_HOME; native formats, locking, throughput, explicit SQLite names and clears remain authoritative. Unreadable manual indexes fail and startup backfill stays unfinished.

Verification: CLI rollout-command tests and local::rollout_migration::tests cover the separate command, unchanged legacy files, read-only dry runs, forced complete projections, ordinary migration, scoped pruning, immutable histories and compressed preservation; metadata::tests cover missing-row titles, existing names, explicit clears and unreadable backfill.


